Here is the MATLAB code to solve for "x":
syms a b c p q r x
eq1 = ap + bq + cr == 28;
eq2 = a + b + c == 10;
eq3 = x == a + 2*b - c/3;
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);
The "sol" variable will contain the solutions for "a", "b", and "c" that can be used to calculate the value of "x".

response:
 To extract the value of "x" from the solutions obtained for "a", "b", and "c", you can substitute these values back into equation (3) as follows:
```MATLAB
% Solving the system of equations for a, b, and c
[sol_abc] = sol.Solutions; % Get the solutions as a cell array
% Extracting the values of a, b, and c from the first solution
[~, idx] = min(abs(sol_abc{1}.Residuals)); % Find the index of the valid solution
a_val = double(sol_abc{1}.Variables.a(idx).Value);
b_val = double(sol_abc{1}.Variables.b(idx).Value);
c_val = double(sol_abc{1}.Variables.c(idx).Value);
% Calculate the value of x
x_val = a_val + 2*b_val - c_val/3;
```
